  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A simple pendulum is displaced by a small angle from its equilibrium position and when released, it oscillates with simple harmonic motion (SHM). The acceleration of the pendulum is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\"></span> and its displacement is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"s\"></span>. Which of the following is the correct relationship between the acceleration and the displacement of the pendulum?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\\: \\alpha\\: s\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\\: \\alpha\\: -s\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\\: \\alpha\\: \\frac{1}{s}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a\\: \\alpha\\: -\\frac{1}{s}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
